{"uid":"1b81cbef8d29e146","name":"test_enter_in_rule_text_inserts_a_newline_and_never_submits","fullName":"tests.test_hub_parked_actions#test_enter_in_rule_text_inserts_a_newline_and_never_submits","historyId":"0735988518987d3762b3e635b72bb3ed","time":{"start":1791959526110,"stop":1791959526110,"duration":0},"description":"`Enter` in a `<textarea>` inserts a newline natively and never\n    triggers implicit form submission (HTML's implicit submission applies\n    to single-line inputs only). So the requirement holds exactly when\n    nothing in app.js overrides it: no key handler on `#rule-text` itself,\n    no key listener anywhere in the bundle that could intercept `Enter` to\n    submit, and the Rule form submits only on its own `submit` event. The\n    panel's own `#parked-rule-text` is likewise a bare `<textarea>` with no\n    key handler at all -- its own submit is only ever the button click.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>Enter</code> in a <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> inserts a newline natively and never<br />\ntriggers implicit form submission (HTML's implicit submission applies<br />\nto single-line inputs only). So the requirement holds exactly when<br />\nnothing in app.js overrides it: no key handler on <code>#rule-text</code> itself,<br />\nno key listener anywhere in the bundle that could intercept <code>Enter</code> to<br />\nsubmit, and the Rule form submits only on its own <code>submit</code> event. The<br />\npanel's own <code>#parked-rule-text</code> is likewise a bare <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> with no<br />\nkey handler at all -- its own submit is only ever the button click.</p>\n","status":"skipped","statusMessage":"Skipped: node not installed","statusTrace":"('/__w/ralphd/ralphd/tests/test_hub_parked_actions.py', 498, 'Skipped: node not installed')","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791959389129,"stop":1